speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the Parties with respect to the visit of Her Majesty Queen Beatrix next week. I think you would find unanimous consent to pass the following motion:
That, notwithstanding Standing Order 3(1), on Tuesday, May 10, 1988, the House shall meet at two o'clock p.m.;
That, for the purpose of the operation of the Standing Orders, such sitting shall be deemed to be a Wednesday, except that Private Members' Business shall be taken up between five o'clock p.m. and six o'clock p.m.;
That, the address of Her Majesty Queen Beatrix of the Netherlands to be delivered in the House Chamber on Tuesday, May 10, 1988, at eleven o'clock a.m., before the Members of the Senate and House of Commons, together with all introductory and related speeches, be printed as an appendix to the House of Commons Debates of that day and form part of the records of this House; and
That, Her Majesty's address, together with all introductory and related remarks, be made available to the media for transmission in the usual way by the House of Commons broadcasting system.
